comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-08T10:32:51.895Z","harness:codex","Partial tranche evidence 2026-08-08: added the public path-redacted host errno classifier/translator/async boundary for EACCES, EDQUOT, EMFILE, ENFILE, ENOMEM, ENOSPC, EPERM, and EROFS; snapshot create/restore now consume it while preserving published snapshot error codes. Generated catalog, negative controls, 22/22 linked tests, security scan, and exact full coverage pass. Acceptance is not complete: the remaining awaited filesystem sites still need routing or explicit waivers and a CI recurrence gate. Returning this item to open and releasing the claim rather than claiming whole-repo completion."
  "2026-08-10T00:19:43.045Z","harness:codex","Live reliability evidence 2026-08-10: the 14-day release gate reports critical=0 and high=1 for Sentry group PM-CLI-2X, an unexpected ENOTDIR open fault. This is another member of the untyped host-filesystem family owned by this item; no duplicate item was created. The active SDK/CLI PR does not claim to complete this item's remaining all-call-site routing and recurrence-gate acceptance criteria, so the item remains open and unclaimed. No paths, payloads, or private endpoint data are retained here."
  "2026-08-17T02:03:50.281Z","harness:codex","Start evidence 2026-08-17: Sentry PM-CLI-36 exposes Linux EDQUOT as code='Unknown system error -122' plus errno=-122 and syscall=copyfile, which the existing shared classifier misses because it recognizes only symbolic code strings. This active partial tranche will normalize declared numeric errno values through node:os constants and wrap linked-test sandbox copy stages in the shared path-redacted boundary. Whole-repository call-site/gate acceptance remains separately outstanding unless completed in this tranche."
  "2026-08-17T02:30:01.217Z","harness:codex","Delivered and verified one additional boundary tranche: the shared classifier now normalizes declared numeric Node errno values, and linked-test tracker seeding uses the path-redacted typed boundary. Exact coverage, focused linked tests, static quality, security, artifact, and consumer smokes pass. The item remains open because its acceptance criteria still require migrating the remaining ad hoc host-filesystem call sites and adding the complete enforcement gate."
  "2026-08-17T05:02:01.000Z","harness:codex","Nightly recurrence evidence 2026-08-17: GH-1048 / run 31995604146 passed 7,450 tests on Windows Node 24 but failed the two newly added numeric-EDQUOT cases because node:os.constants.errno.EDQUOT is absent on Windows, producing NaN and code='Unknown system error -undefined'. This is test-fixture platform coupling in the active host-environment fault tranche, not a failure of symbolic fault translation. Active work will preserve the real Linux -122 negative control while selecting a locally declared numeric errno for cross-platform boundary coverage."
  "2026-08-17T05:18:48.964Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence 2026-08-17: linked host-boundary plans pass 24/24 and 74/74; full repository coverage passes 511 files / 7,459 tests at exact 100/100/100/100 (54,509 statements, 40,594 branches, 11,206 functions, 52,610 lines); typecheck, ESLint, zero-duplicate jscpd, repository assurance, SDK/package/surface/graph gates, secret scan, and isolated SDK/CLI performance gates pass. The broader all-filesystem-boundary/gate acceptance remains outstanding, so this item returns to open rather than being falsely closed."
  "2026-08-17T05:24:46.557Z","harness:codex","Incident delivery update: concrete child pm-y4kovm is implemented in PR #1050 (https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1050), commit 8937ac7c8. The umbrella remains open and unclaimed for broader call-site adoption and recurrence governance; only the concrete child was closed."
  "2026-08-28T16:50:23.597Z","harness:codex","Active tranche 2026-08-28: the v2026.8.28 release blocker exposed raw system-tar failures in the SDK npm-source resolver. This tranche will route registry tarballs through the existing bounded archive validator, reject links/path escapes before extraction, and return typed path-redacted missing-archive diagnostics. The umbrella remains open after this tranche because its all-filesystem-call-site enforcement acceptance is broader."
  "2026-08-28T16:50:57.772Z","harness:codex","TDD red evidence: a registry tarball containing a symbolic link was accepted by the raw system-tar path and fully resolved; the focused suite failed with unsafe registry archive resolved. The same regression also requires a stable npm_package_archive_missing diagnostic when npm reports a filename it did not create. No resolver implementation changed before this negative control."
  "2026-08-28T17:15:14.607Z","harness:codex","Tranche verification 2026-08-28: registry npm tarballs now use the bounded local archive validator before extraction, link/path/type/size controls apply uniformly, and an absent reported artifact returns npm_package_archive_missing without a path or raw tar frame. Linked plans passed 24/24, 76/76, 11/11, and the focused npm package integration slice 6/6. Full repository coverage passed 585 files and 8,089 tests at exact 100/100/100/100: statements 59,999/59,999, branches 45,196/45,196, functions 12,477/12,477, lines 57,778/57,778. Temporary-project pm-changelog registry install and deep doctor passed with zero warnings/errors. The umbrella returns to open because its remaining all-filesystem-site migration and recurrence gate are not complete."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-17T02:30:00.618Z","harness:codex","Node can surface Linux quota exhaustion as code='Unknown system error -122' with errno=-122; portable host-boundary classification must normalize declared numeric node:os.constants.errno values rather than guess numeric literals."
  "2026-08-17T05:06:05.230Z","harness:codex","node:os.constants.errno is platform-specific: EDQUOT is declared on Linux but absent on Windows. Numeric errno tests must choose a locally declared equivalent while retaining the Linux EDQUOT path where available, and lookup tables must filter missing runtime constants before constructing numeric maps."
